  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium morphinan (N-methyl-N-cyclopropylmethyl) with a phenolic OH and ketone; the permanent positive charge is a major barrier to passive oral absorption, and the low-F phenolic/first-pass-liable contexts are the most relevant transfer templates.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C07","C16","C20","C23","C33","C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Multiple transferable human low-F contexts report absolute oral bioavailability below 20%: UK-224,671 3.6% fed and 7.5% fasted; estradiol 4-11%; MK-458 ~4-5%; rotigotine low/essentially none; catechins ~1.7% or modeled F 0.01-0.1.",
      "card_ids": ["C12","C17","C04","C07","C16","C20","C02","C11","C21","C22","C23","C01","C03","C13","C15","C19","C24","C08","C09","C14"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records reinforce the low-F direction: UK-224,671 remained 3.6% fed; estradiol oral bioavailability is ~10% and 1-12%; rotigotine has poor/essentially no oral bioavailability; PHNO is low.",
      "card_ids": ["C25","C31","C36","C33","C37","C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 records show high intestinal absorption for naloxone (95.3% in rat ligated loop; virtually complete) and A275 (0.92-0.99 fraction absorbed in rats), but these are tertiary-amine morphinans or glucuronide conjugates, not the quaternary query; they do not provide affirmative evidence for query F >= 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C58","C62","C54","C55","C56","C59","C61","C63","C64"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The high-F contexts (pethidine F 0.48-0.57, ~50%; rat EC 31-39%) are not transferable because pethidine is a small lipophilic tertiary amine ester lacking the quaternary ammonium charge and phenolic first-pass liabilities, and the rat EC values are species/formulation-specific.",
      "card_ids": ["C05","C06","C10","C18","C30","C26","C29"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63","C64"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus IV AUC data for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific intestinal absorption, solubility, or permeability measurement.",
    "No quaternary ammonium analog data; L4 absorption records are for tertiary-amine morphinans (naloxone) or glucuronide conjugates (A275), not the query.",
    "Ionization behavior at physiological pH is uncertain; the reported neutral fraction (0.97) is inconsistent with the explicit quaternary ammonium charge.",
    "No query-specific formulation, dose, species, or prandial-state data."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query's permanent quaternary ammonium charge and phenolic morphinan scaffold align with multiple transferable low-F contexts (UK-224,671, estradiol, MK-458, rotigotine, catechins), all below 20%; L2 records reinforce this direction, and L4 intestinal absorption records for tertiary-amine analogs are not applicable to the quaternary query. Confidence remains moderate due to lack of direct query measurement."
}

